<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<!--
  One overridden string, and it earns its file.

  The installer closes Windows Explorer and starts it again, which is the one thing about it a
  user cannot guess and would reasonably be alarmed by. There is nowhere else to say so: the
  licence page is the licence, and the progress bar is too late. WixUI declares its own strings
  Overridable, so redefining this one here replaces it.

  The line breaks are character references rather than actual newlines. An XML parser normalises
  a literal newline inside an attribute value to a space, so writing the paragraphs out over
  several lines produces one run-on paragraph in the dialog.
-->

<WixLocalization Culture="en-us" xmlns="http://wixtoolset.org/schemas/v4/wxl">

  <String Id="WelcomeDlgDescription" Value="The Setup Wizard will install [ProductName] on your computer.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Windows Explorer will be closed and restarted during the installation. FlickGit's context menu runs inside Explorer, so this is the only way to replace it — any open Explorer windows will close.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Click Next to continue or Cancel to exit." />

</WixLocalization>
